cff-version: 1.2.0
title: >-
  Korean data-protection enforcement datasets: PIPC sanction
  decisions, dispute mediation, civil damages judgments and
  commencement dates
message: >-
  If you use these tables, please cite them. Where your work has
  to stay checkable, cite a dated snapshot rather than the live
  file — see the README.
type: dataset
authors:
  - family-names: Lee
    given-names: Hyunsub
    affiliation: SEUM Law
repository-code: "https://github.com/swap08/datalaw-data"
url: "https://datalaw.kr/sanctions/"
abstract: >-
  Four tables covering how Korea's personal data laws are
  enforced: sanction decisions published by the Personal
  Information Protection Commission, disputes resolved by the
  Personal Information Dispute Mediation Committee, civil
  judgments on damages for data breaches, and statutes with
  future commencement dates. Built by reading the underlying
  decisions rather than the press releases. Only published
  documents are counted, and many respondents are anonymised,
  so counts are a floor rather than a census.
keywords:
  - data protection
  - privacy law
  - South Korea
  - PIPA
  - Personal Information Protection Commission
  - regulatory enforcement
  - legal empirical research
license: CC-BY-4.0
version: 2026.09.12
date-released: "2026-09-12"
